WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.050
A car pulls away, cruises,
then brakes to a stop.

2
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:05.860
13 seconds in all.

3
00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:08.220
Plot its velocity against time.

4
00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:12.580
Up for 4 seconds, flat for 6, down for 3.

5
00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:16.400
The slope tells you how hard
it speeds up or slows down.

6
00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:18.260
But the car went somewhere.

7
00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:23.380
So on this velocity–time graph,
where is the distance covered hiding?

8
00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:26.580
In this mission, you'll read
displacement–time graphs,

9
00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:29.030
where the gradient is the velocity.

10
00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:32.770
Then you'll watch a velocity–time
line cross the time axis,

11
00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:35.720
and find out what that
crossing really means.

12
00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:40.360
Your mission: find where the distance
covered hides on this kind of graph.
